     "description": "Sergei Fedorov\u2019s brilliance was on full display December 26, 1996, when he single-handedly carried Detroit to victory by scoring all five goals in a thrilling 5\u20134 overtime win against Washington. It was a jaw-dropping showcase of everything that made him special\u2014blazing speed through the neutral zone, a lethal wrist shot, and the ability to rise in the biggest moments. Fedorov was unstoppable, delivering one of the most legendary individual performances in Red Wings history.  \r\nA true two-way superstar, Fedorov became the first Russian-born Hart Trophy winner (1994) and twice claimed the Selke as the NHL\u2019s best defensive forward. He helped power Detroit to three Stanley Cups (1997, 1998, 2002) and was the first Russian player to record 1,000 career points. Inducted into the Hockey Hall of Fame in 2015, Fedorov remains one of the most complete players the game has ever seen.\r\n\r\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
